        "content": "**NOAA GFS 10 m wind** at 0.5°, read live from [PacIOOS ERDDAP](https://pae-paha.pacioos.hawaii.edu/erddap/griddap/ncep_global.html): one CSV request for `u` and `v`, 2,703 cells from 40°S to 12°N, queried with DuckDB. No tile server and no preprocessing.\n\nBoth maps draw **`vectorfield`**, a kepler.gl layer type registered by [this plugin](https://github.com/ubica-ecuador/keplergl-grafana-panel). It takes the same U/V (or speed/direction) columns as its sibling `flowfield`, so changing a layer's type between the two keeps its columns and colour ramp.\n\n- **Top: WMO wind barbs on the data's own cells.** Half barb 5 kn, full barb 10, pennant 50, circle for calm. The feathers sit left of the staff in the northern hemisphere and right of it in the southern: look along the equator.\n- **Bottom: arrows on a screen grid**, sized and coloured by speed, over the flow field traced from the same rows. The grid is laid out in pixels, so the arrows stay legible at any zoom.\n\n**The layer panel on the left of either map is live**: expand a layer to switch *Symbol* (arrow, classified arrow, wind barb), *Placement* (screen grid, data cells) and *Direction is* (where it comes from, where it goes). The picker above chooses the forecast hour.",
        "mode": "markdown"
