          "format": 1,
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "-- NOAA GFS 10 m wind, u and v, in ONE request: 53 x 51 = 2,703 cells.\n--\n-- Every other cell of the 0.5 degree archive, so one per degree -- a regular\n-- lattice, which both velocity layers need: they deduce the spacing from the\n-- coordinates and draw nothing if it wobbles.\n--\n-- `.csv0` has no header and no units row, so read_csv names by position. Only\n-- `[` and `]` need escaping (%5B/%5D). The two subscripts must be written\n-- identically or ERDDAP answers 400.\n--\n-- The hour goes INSIDE a literal, hence `:raw` -- this datasource would\n-- otherwise quote it a second time.\nSELECT column1       AS latitude,\n       column2 - 360 AS longitude,  -- ERDDAP publishes longitude as 0..360\n       -- `u` and `v` are the names the velocity layers look for.\n       column3       AS u,\n       column4       AS v\nFROM read_csv('https://pae-paha.pacioos.hawaii.edu/erddap/griddap/ncep_global.csv0?ugrd10m%5B(${hour:raw})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D,vgrd10m%5B(${hour:raw})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D',\n  header = false,\n  columns = {'column0': 'TIMESTAMP', 'column1': 'DOUBLE', 'column2': 'DOUBLE',\n             'column3': 'DOUBLE', 'column4': 'DOUBLE'},\n  nullstr = 'NaN')\n-- No time column, on purpose: a velocity field holds one instant, and the hour\n-- is fixed by the picker above.\nWHERE column3 IS NOT NULL AND column4 IS NOT NULL\n",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Wind barbs on the data cells · ${hour:text}",
      "type": "ubica-keplergl-panel"
    },
